- User decision on one observer per machine, relayed by the orchestrator (2026-11-23) -- the single instance found through one per-user record, newer-replaces-older over a token-protected shutdown with no event lost, the home view of every project, each session view confined to its project's reported root, and the kanban-folder override scoped to the project it was run from.
- User-settled observer design, relayed by the orchestrator (2026-11-22) -- replay-then-live with dedupe on session and order, Host check, token on every request, file confinement, delete of past sessions only, and no file watching.
- Observer feature parent spec and its event-log child spec (frontmatter) -- the recording side as the logs' only writer, file-first recording, and the rule that a live session cannot be deleted.
